-- 2) 967 deadline alignment + requirements sharpenings (notes append: replay once)
UPDATE scholarships SET deadline = 'Two stages in one application shared with the Axel Adler Scholarship. For the 2027 round: (1) apply for a sustainability-focused master''s programme at the University of Gothenburg as your FIRST choice by 15 January 2027, and pay the application fee and submit entry-requirement documents by 1 February 2027 at universityadmissions.se; (2) the scholarship application itself is by invitation only - eligible applicants receive the invitation by email around 10 February 2027 and must submit between 10 February and 8 March 2027. Results are emailed on 12 April 2027 (master''s). deadline_date stores the scholarship-application close (8 March 2027), as on the main Axel Adler record - but the 15 January first-choice study application is the gate: miss it and no invitation follows.', deadline_date = '2027-03-08', rounds = '[{"round":"2027","study_application_by":"2027-01-15","documents_by":"2027-02-01","invitation":"2027-02-10","scholarship_application":"2027-02-10 to 2027-03-08","results":"2027-04-12","status":"upcoming"},{"pattern":"Annual within the Axel Adler Scholarship round: first-choice sustainability-focused master''s application by mid-January, documents by 1 February, invitation in February, scholarship application window February to early March, results in April; 2-12 awards"}]', application_status = 'upcoming', requirements = REPLACE(REPLACE(requirements, 'i.e. admission to one of the university''s sustainability-focused master''s programmes (bachelor''s programmes and the distance-learning Education for Sustainable Development master''s do not count).', 'i.e. admission to one of the university''s sustainability-focused master''s programmes (bachelor''s programmes and the distance-learning Education for Sustainable Development master''s do not count). Only sustainability-focused programmes qualify: students at sustainability-related programmes cannot be awarded this scholarship.'), 'where selection rests on the CV and letter of motivation written in the scholarship system (maximum 3,000 characters each;', 'where sustainability applicants additionally answer the question "Please motivate why you should receive The Axel Adler Scholarship for Sustainability, in reference to your focus within the area of sustainability" (maximum 3,000 characters), and selection rests on the CV and letter of motivation written in the scholarship system (maximum 3,000 characters each;'), last_verified_at = '2026-10-29 12:00:00+05', last_updated_at = '2026-10-29 12:00:00+05', notes = notes || ' BATCH 32 RECHECK 2026-10-29: the Axel Adler page and BOTH 2027 requirements PDFs were read first-hand - the dedicated sustainability PDF (source 3147) for the first time. The sustainability PDF (at least 2, at most 12 awards in 2027; only sustainability-focused master''s programmes, expressly not sustainability-related ones; Education for Sustainable Development excluded as not campus-based; an extra in-system motivation question of max 3,000 characters; conditions following the main scheme; no living/accommodation cover) publishes no dates of its own and states the application follows the Axel Adler process, so this record now aligns with the main Axel Adler record 739: deadline_date moved from the first-choice study-application deadline (2027-01-15) to the scholarship-application close 2027-03-08 from the main 2027 PDF (submission window 10 February to 8 March 2027, by emailed invitation), the deadline narrative and rounds JSON carry the full two-stage chain, the focused-not-related rule and the extra motivation question were added to requirements, and application_status is aligned to ''upcoming'' as on record 739 (the 15 January study application remains the operational gate).' WHERE id = 967;

